3 to form sequence) and keep B7,B7 as a pair option. This gives me the most outs for completing a winning hand.\n\nReason: Discarding W4 maintains the most flexible hand structure. I keep W1,W1,W2 which can form either a pair (W1,W1) + potential chow, or wait for W3 to complete W1,W2,W3. I also maintain B7,B7 as a pair option. With limited tiles remaining (W3:1, W2:1 unshown), I need to maximize my waiting tiles. This discard keeps my hand closest to a standard 4-meld-1-pair winning pattern.\n\nAnswer: Play W4"}
